values
  (218, 'Changes to slice 4.2 after an independent review, before it merged. A job paused after a run took it does not wake in that run. A job caps itself only if its cap is still the one the run read, so a cap a person just raised is not overwritten. A job is never made active at or over its cap, whether it was capped or paused. Capping and uncapping move a job''s version on, so a page opened before them is refused as changed rather than resuming the job unasked. A job''s history shows its last 100 changes. Left as they are: the list shows each job''s last wake time, not its wakes; jobs have no notes to show yet; a goal may be set for any kind; making briefs wake less often than hourly can skip people''s mornings, which the page does not yet warn of', 'The review found that pausing did not stop a run already under way, that a raised cap could be overwritten by the scheduler, and that pausing then resuming got round the rule against resuming a job over its cap. Each now has a test', 'active', 'the owner', '2026-11-26T00:00:00Z', 'import', '218')
on conflict (origin, origin_ref) where origin_ref is not null do nothing;
